# 2. Area ownership and Machine behavior

Simplify Area behavior to exactly two modes.

## 2.1 Area without Machines

An Area with zero Machines:

* has no queue,
* directly owns and processes received quantity,
* records the Area and Operation,
* keeps `Machine = NULL`,
* shows no placeholder Machine cards,
* shows no “queued” or “on machines” statistics.

## 2.2 Area with Machines

An Area with one or more Machines always uses:

```text
QUEUE_AND_ASSIGN
```

This applies equally to one Machine and multiple Machines.

Rules:

* Newly received quantity enters the Area queue.
* Quantity is assigned explicitly through a one-shot Machine assignment workflow.
* Never auto-assign merely because the Area has one Machine.
* There is no Machine Session.
* One Machine may hold quantities from multiple PNs.
* A queued PN row has an `ASSIGN` action.
* A Machine-assigned PN row has a `QUEUE` action to return quantity to the Area queue.

Remove any configuration or documentation that suggests behavior should differ between one Machine and multiple Machines unless still needed for another confirmed requirement.

