# 7. PN scan resolution cases

## 7.1 PN has no active Work Order Demand

Open an intake flow equivalent to the Work Orders “Add Part” workflow.

Defaults:

```text
Request Type = MODIFY
Route Mode = FLOATING
```

Both remain editable.

The flow must collect or confirm:

* PN,
* quantity,
* Request Type,
* due date,
* reason/notes where applicable,
* Route Mode,
* Planned Route only when `PLANNED`,
* starting/current Area,
* Operation when needed.

On confirmation, the future production transaction will:

1. create or reuse the PartNumber,
2. create or reuse an applicable internal blank-number MODIFY Work Order,
3. create WorkOrderDemand,
4. create QuantityFlow,
5. record the initial Movement,
6. establish current position,
7. place quantity in the Area queue when the Area has Machines,
8. place quantity directly in Area processing when it has no Machines.

The Phase 2 mock must demonstrate this flow without pretending persistence exists.

